FINDING (preamble strengthened this session): the first run_python attempt NARRATED + wrote a
markdown code fence instead of calling the tool. Fix = a firmer _tool_preamble (harness/mcp/tools.py):
"when a tool can do the work, emit the <tool> call INSTEAD of writing code/answer; do NOT use
markdown fences; pass code as a JSON string." After: run_python fires reliably.

KNOWN REFINEMENT (honest negative): multi-line INDENTED code inside a JSON string is unreliable
-- a Fibonacci attempt collapsed indentation (IndentationError; the model even saw the stderr
and retried, proving the feedback loop). One-line programs work cleanly. Follow-ups: a line-list
code arg, or a non-JSON code delimiter, for robust multi-line code. The MECHANISM is solid; the
limiter is the model encoding indented code as a JSON string.

